<task id="136" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>C2 — external read gates test RIGHTS, not key presence: a None-rights root stops admitting reads (including document content download) on both planes, and /me stops leaking None ids</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-30, session 27; contact-plane group, defect C2)</phase>
    <gate>after-135-131</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization gates on live /api/v1/external read routes (.cs), including an app-only file stream; tags bff-api/auth/security.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive: changes the admission rule on every external read route and removes access that null-level grant rows confer today; must not turn C3's cache-hit under-grant into a silent full denial.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Hot-file rule: edits Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs and AccessibleRecordSetService.cs (same files as tasks 135, 137, 138 and 141 — sequence 135 → 136 → 137; serialize with 138/141) and Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs (also consumed by task 140's contact-side grant, which depends on this task).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>135, 131</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, dataverse, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Session 26 verified defect C2 [HIGH] (notes/session26-uac-defects-and-synopsis.md § C2; UC5 "LIKELY DEFECT, OVER-GRANT"; cross-cutting finding 2). Session-26 cross-link: "Fix C3 with or before C2".</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>The external read routes ask "is this record id in the caller's map?" instead of "does the caller hold Read on it?". Two live paths put ids in the map with no rights at all — a Secure-suppressed organization grant and a matter or work-assignment grant row with no level — and those ids still admit project reads, document lists and the app-only document content download. Make every external read gate rights-based, keep None-rights ids out of the principal entirely, and stop /me telling the client about records it holds nothing on.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE BFF security engineer — CallerPrincipal, the evaluator's rights map, and the /api/v1/external read routes. You are removing access on purpose; count what is removed before it ships.</role>

  <goal>On both planes a record reaches the caller's principal only with Read; every /api/v1/external read route and every module scope dimension admits a record only when the caller holds Read on it; `AccessibleRecordSet.Contains` and `IsRecordAccessibleAsync` mean "holds Read"; /me lists only records the caller can read; and the seam tests assert denial (absence), not merely `RightsFor == None`.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>🔴 LIVE, verified 2026-09-30 against source.

THE PRESENCE GATES. `CallerPrincipal.HasProjectAccess` (`Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs:161`) is `ProjectAccess.Any(p =&gt; p.ProjectId == projectId)`; `AccessibleMatterIds` / `AccessibleWorkAssignmentIds` (`:145-149`) and `GetAccessibleProjectIds` (`:152`) are key views. The module scope dimensions consume them unchanged (`Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs:229`, `:250-252`, `:265-266`, `:279`, `:291`), so the module /fetch and /record admit None keys too. The legacy `ExternalCallerContext.HasProjectAccess` (`ExternalCallerContext.cs:43-44`) has the same shape.

THE READ ROUTES THAT GATE ON PRESENCE ONLY (`Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs`): GetProjects lists every key (`:256`); GetProjectById `:273`; GetDocuments `:290`; DownloadDocumentContent `:322`, which then resolves SPE pointers and streams APP-ONLY (`:346-363`); GetDocumentVersions `:694`; GetEvents `:766`; GetContacts `:823`; GetOrganizations `:840`. Contrast the to-do list, which already checks Read (`:399-401`), and the mutating routes, which check Create/Write after a presence check (`:562`/`:570`, `:792`/`:797`). The file header (`:31-34`) claims read routes verify Read; the code does not.

HOW None KEYS GET IN.
1. Workforce plane (and CIAM after task 135): Secure suppression of an organization-only grant. `GrantedRightsFor` maps a null `DirectAccessLevel` to None (`AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:232-234`, `:241-256`), and `AccumulateTerm` inserts the key regardless (`:308-318`); the vetoes remove keys only for deny and Restricted (`:375-406`). `WorkforcePrincipalStrategy` copies every key, None included (`CallerPrincipalResolver.cs:527-529`, `:545-546`).
2. Both planes: matter and work-assignment grant rows with a null `sprk_accesslevel` are kept deliberately as None keys (`ExternalParticipationService.cs:884-907`; the comment calls dropping them a "SILENT REVOCATION"). This only happens for rows written outside the BFF (the BFF always writes a level).

THE /me LEAK. `ExternalUserContextEndpoint.cs:72-76` returns every `ProjectAccess` entry, emitting the level string "None" for a record the caller holds nothing on — the client learns the GUID of a Secure project it cannot read.

THE TESTS PIN THE WRONG THING. Several assertions check only `RightsFor(x).Should().Be(AccessRights.None)`, which is true both when the key is absent and when it is present-but-powerless: `AccessibleRecordSetServiceTests.cs:625, :1377, :1524`; `tests/integration/seam/ExternalAccess/UnifiedEvaluatorSeamTests.cs:167, :397, :632`; `StandingGrantRuntimeUnionSeamTests.cs:163`. (The session-26 note cited :700/:787 and :300/:335; those anchors have drifted.)

WHY C3 FIRST. The grant cache drops `DirectAccessLevel` (C3). Today a cache hit turns a direct grant on a Secure root into a None key that still passes presence reads; after this task it becomes a full denial. Task 131 (C3) must land first so that cannot happen.

THE OWNER RULE THIS ENFORCES. A contact gets ONLY granted records at the granted level; a record with no rights is not a granted record. Task 042 already set the precedent on the standing term: "present but powerless is worse than not accessible" (`AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:1151-1157`).

TASK 070. Its POML (`tasks/070-gate-semantic-search.poml:56`) names the ExternalProjectDataEndpoints project-access-plus-document-scoping check as the reference implementation to copy. Its shipped code does NOT spread the defect — it gates on a Read snapshot (`Api/Filters/SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.cs:500`, `Api/Ai/SemanticSearchEndpoints.cs:572`). ⚠️ 070 was ALREADY amended on 2026-09-30 (an amendments block: reference withdrawn, deps `046, 136`, "the reference to copy is task 136's rights-based gate"). This task does not add a second amendment; it re-verifies that block's claims and anchors once its own gate exists.

TASKS 037 AND 039. Both were re-opened 2026-09-30; their status-notes return them to completed only when BOTH 135 and 136 are completed, and their amended acceptance criteria (including a manual CIAM live gate) name this task as the completing work for the C2 half. Closing them is part of this task.</background>
