  <constraints>
    <constraint source="C2 fix direction / ADR-003">Scope: the principal (both strategies). A record enters `ProjectAccess`, `MatterAccess` or `WorkAssignmentAccess` only when its rights include Read. Prune at construction AND make `HasProjectAccess` and the three `GetAccessible*Ids` / `Accessible*Ids` views require Read — two independent layers, so a future construction path that forgets to prune still fails closed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C2 fix direction">Scope: the evaluator. `AccessibleRecordSet.Contains` (`AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:149`) and `IsRecordAccessibleAsync` (`:749-760`) answer "holds Read". Removing None-valued keys at the end of each composition (after the veto pipeline) is the preferred shape — a veto already removes keys, and absence is the only representation of no access. Do not introduce any value that means "denied".</constraint>
    <constraint source="C2 fix direction">Scope: every /api/v1/external read route listed in the background (`:256`, `:273`, `:290`, `:322`, `:694`, `:766`, `:823`, `:840`). Each denies with the existing 403 ProblemDetails unless the caller holds Read on the record; GetProjects lists only Read-bearing projects. The content download must deny BEFORE any SPE pointer resolution or Graph read (keep the authz-before-stream order at `:320-346`). Mutating routes keep their existing Create/Write checks.</constraint>
    <constraint source="hot-file coordination">Scope: the module seam. Do NOT edit `ExternalModuleRegistry.cs` or `ExternalAccessModule.cs` (task 134 owns them); the module dimensions become rights-based through the `CallerPrincipal` views they already read.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner model 2026-09-30">Scope: null-level matter/WA grant rows. They stop conferring access (no level = not granted). This REMOVES live access: count and list the affected rows in dev before merging (see escalation). Update the "SILENT REVOCATION" comment at `ExternalParticipationService.cs:884-889` so it records the owner decision instead of the old rationale; do not otherwise change the grant query (C12 and task 137 own that file's other changes).</constraint>
    <constraint source="/me">Scope: `ExternalUserContextEndpoint.cs`. /me returns only Read-bearing projects; the "None" branch at `:75` becomes unreachable and a test pins that no entry with level "None" is ever emitted. The test drives the real handler (or the contract host), not a copy of its projection lambda — `CallerPrincipalTests.cs:116-118` is such a copy and proves nothing about the handler; replace it or delete it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. Every security-suppression and veto test that today asserts `RightsFor == None` must ALSO assert the record is absent (`Contains == false` / not in `RecordIds` / not in the principal). Reads must be asserted DENIED at the route (403), not inferred from the map. KEEP paths only; no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration or ctor null-check tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-10 / spec">Scope: verification. No Dataverse test in CI; the live check is a MANUAL gate with existing test users and an existing CIAM test contact; no user relocation; Secure test records created through the provisioning endpoint.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement decision citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; publish size from fresh master and fresh branch worktrees at SHORT paths, Compress-Archive on both, equal file counts, both sizes and the delta reported; ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

