  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Re-verify every anchor. Confirm task 135 and the C3 cache task are merged; if the C3 task is not, fire the escalation.</step>
    <step order="1">Measure the before-state in dev: count and list (a) matter/WA grant rows (contact AND organization rows) with a null `sprk_accesslevel` that are active and unexpired, and (b) organization-only grants on Secure roots. These are the records whose read access this task removes. Also enumerate, by grep, every consumer of `AccessibleRecordSet.Contains` / `.RecordIds` / `.Rights`, `IsRecordAccessibleAsync`, `CallerPrincipal.HasProjectAccess` and the `GetAccessible*Ids` / `Accessible*Ids` views across `src/server/**`, and record the list: each one's behaviour changes from presence to Read, and each must be covered by a test or named as unaffected in the notes.</step>
    <step order="2">Make the evaluator and the principal rights-based (both layers, both strategies), then switch every read route listed to a Read test and GetProjects to Read-bearing ids only; fix /me.</step>
    <step order="3">Update the tests that assert only `RightsFor == None` so they also assert absence; add route-level denial tests; add perturbations.</step>
    <step order="4">Re-verify the existing 2026-09-30 amendment in `tasks/070-gate-semantic-search.poml` against the code after this task (its anchors into `CallerPrincipalResolver.cs` and `ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs` will have moved; correct line numbers in place and add one dated line "task 136 gate delivered DATE"). Correct the stale premise in `notes/task-029-external-todo-parity.md:248-250`. Then close tasks 037 and 039: confirm task 135 is completed, run each task's amended acceptance criteria (the manual CIAM live gate may reuse this task's and 135's recorded evidence where it is the same observation — cite it), append a dated completion line to each amendments block, set both POML statuses to completed and their TASK-INDEX rows to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="5">Build, full suite, seam suite, ArchTests, publish size; MANUAL live gate; notes at `projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-136-rights-based-read-gates.md`; TASK-INDEX and POML status; `check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Task 131 (C3 grant cache) has not merged. STOP — without it, a legitimate direct grant on a Secure root becomes a full denial on every cache hit once presence stops admitting reads.</trigger>
    <trigger>OWNER DECISION if Step 1 finds ANY active, unexpired null-level matter/WA grant row that is not test data: STOP and report the list — back-fill a level (and which) or let them lapse. RECOMMENDATION: let them lapse (no level = not granted), consistent with the owner's C9 rule ("only those records to which granted access … the privileges … as set in the grant access") and with task 107's owner-approved precedent that an undated grant confers nothing; a back-fill would invent a level nobody chose. If every such row is test data, record that and proceed.</trigger>
    <trigger>A read route turns out to need a right other than Read (for example a route that is really a mutation in disguise). STOP and name it rather than choosing the right silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>

