  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Workforce contact with only an organization grant on Secure project P: P is absent from the composed set and the principal, and GET /projects/P, /projects/P/documents, /projects/P/documents/{d}/content, /projects/P/documents/{d}/versions, /projects/P/events, /projects/P/contacts and /projects/P/organizations each return 403 — and the content route makes no SPE pointer or Graph call (asserted).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The same scenario on the CIAM plane (after task 135) gives the same denials.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A matter or work-assignment grant row with a null level confers nothing: the record is absent from `MatterAccess` / `WorkAssignmentAccess` on both planes, and the module /fetch for its documents and invoices returns 0 rows for it, and /record for it returns 403.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Positive: a direct ViewOnly grant on a Secure record still admits every read route (Read is present) and still refuses the mutating routes (no Create/Write).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`AccessibleRecordSet.Contains` and `IsRecordAccessibleAsync` return false for a record whose composed rights lack Read; no composed set contains a None-valued key after composition (pinned by test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Defence in depth: a `CallerPrincipal` constructed directly with a None-rights project (bypassing pruning) still fails `HasProjectAccess` and is excluded from `GetAccessibleProjectIds` / `GetAccessibleMatterIds` / `GetAccessibleWorkAssignmentIds`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /me, driven through the real `ExternalUserContextEndpoint` handler, never returns a project the caller cannot read and never emits the level string "None" (fixture: one Read-bearing project and one None-rights project on the principal; only the first is returned).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every previously `RightsFor == None`-only assertion for a Secure-suppressed, vetoed or null-level record now also asserts absence.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Regression: callers with ordinary grants and systemusers with membership keep every read they had; the to-do and mutating-route tests pass unmodified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Perturbation: restoring presence-only `HasProjectAccess`, removing construction-time pruning, or removing the evaluator's end-of-composition pruning each turns at least one test red (the two layers are proven independent). All reverted before completion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Step 1 before-state (both counts plus the row lists) is recorded in the task notes before merge.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MANUAL live gate (dev, no CI): with an existing CIAM test contact whose organization holds a grant on a Secure project (provisioned through the endpoint) and no direct grant, the external SPA does not list the project, /me does not return its id, and a direct request for one of its documents' content returns 403; adding a direct ViewOnly grant restores read-only access. Evidence in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Task 070's existing amendment is re-verified with corrected anchors and a dated delivery line (no second amendments block); `notes/task-029-external-todo-parity.md:248-250` is corrected.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every consumer found by the Step 1 grep is listed in the task notes with either the test that covers its new Read semantics or a one-line reason it is unaffected.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tasks 037 and 039: their amended acceptance criteria are each evidenced in the task notes, their amendments blocks carry a dated completion line, their POML status is completed and their TASK-INDEX rows are `✅ [done]`; `check-task-status-drift.ps1` reports no drift for 037, 039 or 136. If task 135 is not completed, this criterion fails and 136 is not complete.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build green; full BFF unit suite, seam suite and ArchTests green; publish size reported (both sizes, delta, zip tool, file counts) and ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Defect C2 [HIGH]. Pairs: C1 (task 135) must run first on the same files; C3 (cache) must land first or this task converts an intermittent under-grant into a hard one. After this task, the only remaining source of a None key is none at all — absence is the single representation of no access across evaluator, principal, module seam and /me.

The header at `ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:31-34` becomes true; keep it and cite this task.

Related: tasks 029, 032, 037, 039, 042, 070, 107, 131, 135, 137, 138, 140 (contact-side grant depends on this task: a None-rights key must never read as a grantable root).</notes>

